omx-dsp (0.34.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * release: omx-dsp 0.34.2 (0.34.1 to 0.34.2), a patch
  * The contract directory has no schema-major level: omx-dsp is
    <contractdir>/omx-dsp/
  * release: a merge to devel publishes the real package to staging
  * eq-design-twin: the nine kinds keep their codes, peaking 0 through
    allpass2 8 (#170)
  * ci.yml: the wasm job installs diffutils; wasm-sabotage.sh refuses to run
    without cmp
  * ci.yml: devel green again (cmp in the contract job, dB in the wasm loader
    check, fuzz-sabotage on a readable tree)
  * publish.yml: only the dry-run-only promote jobs may be skipped; every
    other promote job must succeed
  * publish.yml: a skipped dry-run-only promote job passes the npm gate; the
    channel jobs must each succeed
  * release.yml: a tag promotes the staged build through promote-staged.yml,
    it never rebuilds
  * BIQUAD_KINDS goes: enum omx_eq_kind reads its codes from omx-contract's
    PARAM_FILTER_RESPONSES
  * face-descriptor-check reads the kernel unit as its PARAM_UNITS id; three
    fuzz records cite their lines again
  * .githooks/commit-msg is the shared stub, byte for byte
  * Wave review fixes: the render stages omx-contract's domains, units-check
    reads "standard id", the clipper knee's home, the 0.34.1 changelog
  * ci: spdx-check, deps-render and no-floor-check run in a lint job, never
    before make test
  * packaging, build, CI: no hand-kept omx-contract floor;
    tools/no-floor-check.sh refuses one
  * unit enumerators: the C names follow the PARAM_UNITS title (_DB, _DBFS,
    _DBU, _DBTP, _KHZ)
  * data: no file states a schema floor; requires goes where it names nothing
  * kernels: the leveler's and the balancer's speed travel in dBPerS
  * tests: a rate in dB per second states dBPerS, a slope in dB per octave
    dBPerOct (red)
  * The clipper's drive arm keeps its parameter read (#97)
  * README names the generic face's spec (#97)
  * The clipper and width perturbation arms aim at the shared bodies (#97)
  * One copy of each body: the clipper's block and the width's redesign
    shared by both faces (#97)
  * The generic face over a kernel descriptor, first batch trim, width and
    clipper (#97)
  * docs: the kernel and primitive words are this library's, not
    omx-contract's (sorting pass, row V30)
  * fdelay: the read's L1 norm is this library's value, its oracle the kernel
    (sorting pass, row V30)
  * The generic face's tests, red first: descriptor against kernel file, face
    against hand-written face (#97)
  * The generic face specified: one face from a kernel descriptor (#97)
  * tests: FDELAY_READ_L1_NORM is this library's value, held by its kernel
    (red first, row V30)
  * packaging: the omx-contract floor is 3.22.0, the first with the coef unit
    data/ uses (#156)
  * make rtsan: the RealtimeSanitizer probe kept as a dev tool, with a
    self-test that must see a planted usleep (#98)
  * tools: retire the TypeScript golden tools, C is the only source of their
    numbers
  * packaging: the rpm builds the npm tree under Node 26; the deb keeps the
    archive's Node (#147)
  * fx/ and analysis/ state the contracts their bodies evaluate; doc-check
    holds them (#146)
  * contract tests: the omx-contract checkout holds no release fixtures
  * docs-sabotage: the swap arm is built on the listed probe, so it holds at
    an empty baseline (#70)
  * The remaining effect headers and the key documented: baseline 140 to 0
    (#70)
  * release.yml: no dispatch publish input; the release jobs publish on a tag
    push alone
  * The harmonic resonance pass's tracker, baseline and correction, and the
    RTA headers documented: baseline 250 to 140 (#70)
  * Six effect instances' headers documented: baseline 367 to 250 (#70)
  * The harmonic resonance pass's pitch, render and LV2 headers documented:
    baseline 461 to 367 (#70)
  * The feedback suppressor's headers documented: baseline 570 to 461 (#70)
  * Nine instances' atom and state members documented: baseline 587 to 570
    (#70)
  * The instances' ready, sr and enabled members documented: baseline 645 to
    587 (#70)
  * Struct members whose plain comment already documented them are doc
    comments: baseline 682 to 645 (#70)
  * {@link} to the generated defines is plain text: baseline 688 to 682 (#70)
  * The instances' CHANNELS and LATENCY_FRAMES defines documented: baseline
    715 to 688 (#70)
  * The doc blocks the stage define hid reach their functions, with every
    parameter: baseline 742 to 715 (#70)
  * curve, meter: the unit words are the PARAM_UNITS ids, no lowercase copy
  * doc-check: only what doxygen cannot check, a body's contracts stated
  * curve: the band role prefix is declared, with a predicate in C and TS
  * docs: the fuzz README's record and the reverb allpasses' bounds are true
  * ci: every workflow Node is 26, held by tools/ci-node-26.sh
  * tests: the denormal arm puts back the float mode, clamps judged in it
  * curve: an EQ frequency at or below 0 Hz is refused, not drawn flat
  * C2: omxdsp_definitions.h re-rendered from the ids
  * make docs-site and docs.yml: the API reference published per release
    under /reference/omx-dsp/ (Open-Mixer/.github#242)
  * tests: a curve term's unit is its PARAM_UNITS id, "Hz" and "dB" are read
    (red)
  * C2: every unit data/ and recipes/answers/ state is the PARAM_UNITS id
  * units-check: every unit data/ and recipes/answers/ state is a PARAM_UNITS
    symbol
  * release: omx-dsp 0.34.1 (0.34.0 to 0.34.1), a patch
  * rotary: ROTARY_ACCEL_RANGE travels in coef, not "x"
  * ci: the make-test, contract-floor and rpm jobs take their cells from
    check-matrix, on main's ci.yml
  * ci: fedora-cells over the workflows, red on the fc44-only jobs

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:06:05 +0000
